NAME
       nsenter - run a program in the namespaces of another process

SYNOPSIS
       nsenter -t PID [-u] [-m] [-p] [-i] [-n] [-U] [-C] [-T] [--] [COMMAND [ARG]...]

DESCRIPTION
       Join the namespaces of process PID through /proc/PID/ns and run
       COMMAND. Without COMMAND, run $SHELL (or /bin/sh). Requires root.

OPTIONS
       -t, --target PID
           process whose namespaces to join

       -u, --uts
           join the UTS namespace

       -m, --mount
           join the mount namespace

       -p, -i, -n, -U, -C, -T
           accepted, but report that the namespace is not supported yet

EXAMPLES
       sudo nsenter -t 12 -u hostname

SEE ALSO
       unshare(1), hostname(1)
